// §4.5.7 states absdelay as a formula over all past time,
//
//     Output(t) = Input(max(t - td, 0))
//
// and bounds no lookback. VerA keeps the last 1024 accepted samples of each
// absdelay site (docs/Vague_Decisions.md). A delay that reaches past the oldest
// one cannot be answered, and the limit has to fail loudly: the run ends with
// E1012 and exit status 1, never a shorter delay reported as this one
// (a04_05_absdelay_history_beyond_capacity.va pins a lookback the ring holds).
//
// THE SHAPE is a01_08_transcendental_domain_runtime_error.va's: the exit
// status is part of the oracle.
//
// HAND DERIVATION. The input is the ramp $abstime*1e9, td = 1026ns, on a 1ns
// grid 0 .. 1026ns. For every t < td, max(t - td, 0) = 0, so Output = Input(0)
// = 0 and the check prints ok=1 at t = 0 .. 1024ns (1025 points). The operator
// runs before the current point is recorded, so at t = 1025ns the ring holds
// the 1025 samples 0 .. 1024ns less the oldest, 1 .. 1024ns, and Input(0) is
// gone. The run ends there with E1012 and status 1; t = 1025ns prints nothing.
//
// A silent ring fails too: answering from the oldest retained sample gives
// Input(1ns) = 1 at t = 1025ns, and the check prints ok=0.
//
//! lrm 4.5.7
//! bias V(n) = 0
//! exit 1
//! time 0, 1n, 2n, 3n, 4n, 5n, 6n, 7n, 8n, 9n, 10n, 11n, 12n, 13n, 14n, 15n, 16n, 17n, 18n, 19n, 20n, 21n, 22n, 23n, 24n, 25n, 26n, 27n, 28n, 29n, 30n, 31n, 32n, 33n, 34n, 35n, 36n, 37n, 38n, 39n, 40n, 41n, 42n, 43n, 44n, 45n, 46n, 47n, 48n, 49n, 50n, 51n, 52n, 53n, 54n, 55n, 56n, 57n, 58n, 59n, 60n, 61n, 62n, 63n, 64n, 65n, 66n, 67n, 68n, 69n, 70n, 71n, 72n, 73n, 74n, 75n, 76n, 77n, 78n, 79n, 80n, 81n, 82n, 83n, 84n, 85n, 86n, 87n, 88n, 89n, 90n, 91n, 92n, 93n, 94n, 95n, 96n, 97n, 98n, 99n, 100n, 101n, 102n, 103n, 104n, 105n, 106n, 107n, 108n, 109n, 110n, 111n, 112n, 113n, 114n, 115n, 116n, 117n, 118n, 119n, 120n, 121n, 122n, 123n, 124n, 125n, 126n, 127n, 128n, 129n, 130n, 131n, 132n, 133n, 134n, 135n, 136n, 137n, 138n, 139n, 140n, 141n, 142n, 143n, 144n, 145n, 146n, 147n, 148n, 149n, 150n, 151n, 152n, 153n, 154n, 155n, 156n, 157n, 158n, 159n, 160n, 161n, 162n, 163n, 164n, 165n, 166n, 167n, 168n, 169n, 170n, 171n, 172n, 173n, 174n, 175n, 176n, 177n, 178n, 179n, 180n, 181n, 182n, 183n, 184n, 185n, 186n, 187n, 188n, 189n, 190n, 191n, 192n, 193n, 194n, 195n, 196n, 197n, 198n, 199n, 200n, 201n, 202n, 203n, 204n, 205n, 206n, 207n, 208n, 209n, 210n, 211n, 212n, 213n, 214n, 215n, 216n, 217n, 218n, 219n, 220n, 221n, 222n, 223n, 224n, 225n, 226n, 227n, 228n, 229n, 230n, 231n, 232n, 233n, 234n, 235n, 236n, 237n, 238n, 239n, 240n, 241n, 242n, 243n, 244n, 245n, 246n, 247n, 248n, 249n, 250n, 251n, 252n, 253n, 254n, 255n, 256n, 257n, 258n, 259n, 260n, 261n, 262n, 263n, 264n, 265n, 266n, 267n, 268n, 269n, 270n, 271n, 272n, 273n, 274n, 275n, 276n, 277n, 278n, 279n, 280n, 281n, 282n, 283n, 284n, 285n, 286n, 287n, 288n, 289n, 290n, 291n, 292n, 293n, 294n, 295n, 296n, 297n, 298n, 299n, 300n, 301n, 302n, 303n, 304n, 305n, 306n, 307n, 308n, 309n, 310n, 311n, 312n, 313n, 314n, 315n, 316n, 317n, 318n, 319n, 320n, 321n, 322n, 323n, 324n, 325n, 326n, 327n, 328n, 329n, 330n, 331n, 332n, 333n, 334n, 335n, 336n, 337n, 338n, 339n, 340n, 341n, 342n, 343n, 344n, 345n, 346n, 347n, 348n, 349n, 35